    "result_text": "The build is green: all tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the structured audit event in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`, alongside the existing human-readable audit line.\n\n**What was added** (`src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`):\n\n1. **A monotonic sequence** \u2014 `AUDIT_SEQUENCE`, a process-wide `AtomicInteger` incremented once per successful create, so each event's `seq` strictly increases across creates.\n\n2. **`emitOwnerCreatedEvent(Owner)`** \u2014 called right after the existing `AUDIT.info(...)` line (so only successful creates emit it, after the owner is saved and has an id). It builds the event and logs it via the `AUDIT` logger.\n\n3. **`primaryIdentifier(Owner)`** \u2014 a single indirection returning `owner.getCustomerCode()` today. This is the one place to change when the customer code is later unified into the member id, so the event will carry the `memberId` instead \u2014 exactly as the spec requires.\n\n4. **`OwnerCreatedEvent`** \u2014 an immutable `record` carrying `seq`, `ownerId`, `customerCode` (the current primary identifier), and `membershipLevel`. Its `toJson()` serializes to the compact JSON object `{seq, ownerId, customerCode, membershipLevel, event:'OWNER_CREATED'}` (fields in that order) using a shared Jackson `ObjectMapper`.\n\nThe emitted line looks like:\n```\n{\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```\n\nThe acceptance test `coreEventCarriesIdAndIdentifier` passes, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1/1 tests, 0 failures). The immutability (record), the `customerCode` field named as the primary identifier, and the single `primaryIdentifier` switch point together satisfy the forward-compatibility requirement about the identifier becoming the `memberId` later.",
